
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

Run the host-side tests from the PlatformIO terminal with:

    pio test -e native

The native environment compiles only alarm_logic.cpp and system_state.cpp,
so these deterministic decision-logic tests need no ESP32 or Wokwi hardware.
test_logic contains 13 cases: five temperature threshold cases, four display
navigation cases (including both wrap directions), and four system-state
cases (before timeout, timeout reached, remaining inactive, and motion wake).
